+# Feature Specification: Availability
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-17 | **Status**: Implemented
+**Input**: The desk needs to see what can still be rented: `availability({start, end, kind?})` returns the sorted ids of equipment (of that kind, or any) free for the whole period.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: `availability` returns ids of items with no booking overlapping the period (half-open, as in `book`), sorted.
+- **FR-002**: `kind` is optional; when given, only items of that kind are listed.
+- **FR-003**: Invalid periods (same rules as `quote`/`book`) or an invalid kind throw; no items → `[]`.
+
+## Plan / Tasks
+- Add `AvailabilityQuery` and `availability` in `src/index.ts`, reusing `parsePeriod` and the overlap rule of `book`.
+- Add tests in `test/rental.test.ts` (kind filter, back-to-back, sorting, empty, invalid input).
+
+## Assumptions
+- Back-to-back periods do not conflict; a bad `kind` is an error, consistent with `addEquipment`.
